.TH MKV2MP4 1 "October 2026" "mkv2mp4 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mkv2mp4 \- convert MKV files into MP4s that every Jellyfin client can direct play
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkv2mp4
.RI [ options ]
.I source
.I dest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkv2mp4
scans
.I source
for
.B .mkv
files and writes a
.B .mp4
for each one into
.IR dest .
The output plays without server-side transcoding on Jellyfin's web client,
Roku, Fire TV, Apple TV and Android TV.
.PP
For each file
.IR source / path / name .mkv:
.IP 1. 4
.IR dest / path / name .mp4
is created. Subdirectories are mirrored, so
.I Show/Season 01/
keeps the layout Jellyfin expects.
.IP 2. 4
Only after the conversion succeeds, the original is renamed in place to
.IR name .converted.mkv.
Originals are never deleted.
.IP 3. 4
Files already named
.B *.converted.mkv
are skipped, so it is safe to run
.B mkv2mp4
repeatedly, for example from cron. To convert a file again, rename it back to
.BR .mkv .
.PP
.I source
may also be a single
.B .mkv
file. Hidden files and directories (names starting with a dot) are ignored.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.TP
.B Video
H.264 High profile, 8-bit 4:2:0.
Video that is already compatible H.264 is copied unchanged, which is fast and
lossless. Anything else (HEVC, 10-bit, AV1, MPEG-2, VC-1, ...) is re-encoded.
HDR (PQ/HLG) is tone-mapped to SDR BT.709, and interlaced video is
deinterlaced.
.TP
.B Audio
The first track is AAC stereo and is marked default, so every client has
something it can play. It is made from the source's default audio track.
AAC, AC3, E-AC3 and MP3 tracks are copied. Other surround tracks (DTS,
TrueHD, FLAC, PCM, ...) are converted to AC3 at 640 kb/s (7.1 is downmixed to
5.1). Other stereo or mono tracks become AAC. All languages are kept, and
converted tracks are titled
.I "Stereo (AAC)"
or
.IR "Surround (AC3)" .
.TP
.B Subtitles
Text subtitles (SRT, ASS/SSA, WebVTT) are embedded as MP4 text tracks
(ASS styling is lost), or written as sidecar files with
.BR \-\-external\-subs .
Image subtitles (PGS, VobSub, DVB) cannot be stored in MP4. They are dropped
with a warning unless
.B \-\-burn\-subs
is given.
.TP
.B Other
Chapters and global metadata are kept. The index is moved to the front of the
file (faststart) so playback starts immediately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show the plan for every file (what is copied, what is re-encoded, which
tracks are kept) without converting or renaming anything.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " \fIN\fR"
Convert
.I N
files in parallel (default 1). Live progress is shown only when
.I N
is 1.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-encoder " \fIauto\fR|\fIvaapi\fR|\fInvenc\fR|\fIvideotoolbox\fR|\fIx264\fR"
Video encoder. The default,
.BR auto ,
test-encodes at startup and picks NVIDIA NVENC, then VAAPI (Intel/AMD), then
the CPU encoder x264. On macOS it picks VideoToolbox, then x264. Naming a GPU
encoder that doesn't work is an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-vaapi\-device " path"
VAAPI render node (default
.IR /dev/dri/renderD128 ).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quality " \fIN\fR"
Video quality. Lower is better and bigger. Used as the CRF for x264, CQ for
NVENC and QP for VAAPI; VideoToolbox gets a quality of 100 \(mi 2\fIN\fR
(default 20). Sensible range is 18\(en24.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " name"
x264 preset (default
.BR medium ).
Slower presets give smaller files at the same quality.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-height " px"
Downscale video taller than
.I px
(e.g. 1080). This forces a re-encode. Useful for older Fire TV and Roku
devices that cannot play 4K H.264.
.TP
.B \-\-external\-subs
Write text subtitles next to the MP4 as
.IR name . lang [.forced][.default].srt
(or
.BR .ass ,
keeping styling), which Jellyfin picks up automatically, instead of embedding
them.
.TP
.B \-\-burn\-subs
Burn one image subtitle track into the video: the forced track if there is
one, otherwise the default track, otherwise the first. This forces a
re-encode.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rename
Leave the original filenames unchanged. Later runs will then convert the file
again unless the MP4 already exists in
.IR dest .
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Replace MP4s that already exist in
.IR dest .
Without this they are skipped and the original is left alone.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-recursive
Only process the top level of
.IR source .
.TP
.BI \-\-log " file"
Append a log, including every ffmpeg command and any errors, to
.I file
(default
.IR ~/.local/state/mkv2mp4/mkv2mp4.log ).
No log is written for
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH SAFETY
Output is written to a hidden
.IR . name .mp4.part
file and renamed only when ffmpeg succeeds. If a conversion fails or is
interrupted with Ctrl-C, the partial file is removed and the original keeps
its name, so the next run retries it.
.PP
If
.I dest
appears to have less free space than the total size of the input, a warning
is printed but the run continues.
.SH GPU ENCODING
GPU encoding is much faster than x264 but is optional.
.TP
.B Ubuntu
Add yourself to the
.B render
group
.RB ( "sudo usermod \-aG render $USER" ,
then log out and back in) and install
.B mesa\-va\-drivers
(AMD) or
.B intel\-media\-va\-driver
(Intel).
.B mkv2mp4
prints a hint if the render node exists but isn't accessible.
.TP
.B Arch
AMD works with mesa. Intel needs
.B intel\-media\-driver
(or
.B libva\-intel\-driver
for pre-Broadwell chips). NVIDIA needs
.BR nvidia\-utils .
.TP
.B macOS
Apple Silicon Macs use the VideoToolbox hardware encoder with nothing extra to
install. Intel Macs fall back to x264, because VideoToolbox's constant-quality
mode needs Apple Silicon.
.PP
The encoder chosen is shown at the start of every run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All files converted (or nothing to do).
.TP
.B 1
One or more files failed or could not be read.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, missing ffmpeg/ffprobe, or a requested encoder is unavailable.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview what would happen:
.PP
.RS
mkv2mp4 \-n ~/Downloads/rips /srv/jellyfin/Movies
.RE
.PP
Convert, using two parallel jobs on the CPU at a slightly higher quality:
.PP
.RS
mkv2mp4 \-e x264 \-j 2 \-q 19 ~/Downloads/rips /srv/jellyfin/Movies
.RE
.PP
Convert a 4K TV library for older devices, with sidecar subtitles:
.PP
.RS
mkv2mp4 \-\-max\-height 1080 \-\-external\-subs /mnt/rips/TV /srv/jellyfin/TV
.RE
.SH NOTES
If
.I source
is inside a Jellyfin library, Jellyfin will also list the
.B .converted.mkv
files. Keep
.I source
outside your libraries, or move the originals once you are happy with the
results.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mkv2mp4/mkv2mp4.log
Default log file
.RB ( $XDG_STATE_HOME
is honoured).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, disables coloured output.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
